approach was taken to INCLUDE when there was reasonable evidence of randomization and meeting other criteria.
- Confidence levels were assigned as:
  * high: when the study clearly met all inclusion criteria
  * medium: when some uncertainty existed (e.g., quasi-randomization, implicit PFMT inclusion)
  * low: when minimal information was available but exclusion was clear
